        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF153 adds support for the <a href=\"https://github.com/tc39/proposal-iterator-includes\">TC39 Iterator proposal</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2025779\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2025779</a> behind pref <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.options.experimental.iterator_includes</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the feature for the <code class=\"notranslate\">Iterator.includes()</code> builtin.<br>\nNote, I can't see evidence it is supported yet by anyone other than FF, which seems reasonable given it is early in the cycle.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It fails because of the spec url which is the github repo.<br>\nI tried <a href=\"https://tc39.es/proposal-iterator-includes/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tc39.es/proposal-iterator-includes/</a> as well but that didn't work.<br>\nI'm after advice, since it looks in the browser spec repo that tc39 specs are allowed ....</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4469264809\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44158\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44158/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44158\">mdn/content#44158</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29746",
            "title": "FF152 TC39 Iterator includes",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-26T05:05:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T05:04:54.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF152 adds support for importing text modules in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854</a> (this uses the <code class=\"notranslate\">with</code> clause <code class=\"notranslate\">{type: \"text\"}</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the text type subfeature, and corresponding <code class=\"notranslate\">text</code> destination for fetch requests. This doesn't seem to be supported in Chrome or Safari (quick search). I've set other platforms to false, except for BUN</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4470056163\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44166\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44166/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44166\">mdn/content#44166</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29745",
            "title": "FF152 with clause {type: \"text\"}",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-26T02:57:54.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T02:57:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35173023?u=c32269fffe4bd6451bfd635c7fb7d42185edf93c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds to the data that Node 26.0.0 supports <code class=\"notranslate\">[Weak]Map.getOrInsert[Computed]</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Iterator.concat</code></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Running the following code in Node.js 26.0.0 outputs the expected results:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"console.log(new Map().getOrInsert(&quot;key&quot;, &quot;val&quot;));\nconsole.log(Array.from(Iterator.concat([1], [2])));\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Map</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">getOrInsert</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"key\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"val\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-v\">Array</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">from</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-v\">Iterator</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">concat</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is noted in the <a href=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v26.0.0\">Node.js 26.0.0 Changelog</a> under the \"V8 14.6\" section.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29742",
            "title": "Node.js 26.0.0 Upsert and Iterator sequencing",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-25T10:43:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-25T10:42:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ginnyTheCat",
                "url": "https://github.com/ginnyTheCat"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 150 adds support for the <a href=\"https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#dom-speechrecognitionoptions-quality\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">SpeechRecognitionOptions</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code> property</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> object overall, and then a subdata point for <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code>, for both methods that use this <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> object — <code class=\"notranslate\">available()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">install()</code>. I am not 100% sure about this structure, but I copied it from </p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/c0772004be4201be3fd9e0de1099998bc0654e9c/javascript/builtins/Intl/NumberFormat.json#L229\">browser-compat-data/javascript/builtins/Intl/NumberFormat.json</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n         Line 229\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/commit/c0772004be4201be3fd9e0de1099998bc0654e9c\">c077200</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L229\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"229\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC229\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-ent\">\"options_parameter\"</span>: { </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n.<p></p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29741",
