        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 142 adds support for the SVG <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;a&gt;</code> element <a href=\"https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/linking.html#AElementDownloadAttribute\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">download</code> attribute</a>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6265596395913216\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6265596395913216</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We already have up-to-date data for the <code class=\"notranslate\">SVGAElement.download</code> property, but not the SVG <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;a&gt;</code> element <code class=\"notranslate\">download</code> attribute. This PR rectifies that.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
